Q: Test if route exists in Twig Template (Symfony 2) A: <p>You can make a custom twig function (check <a href="http://symfony.com/doc/current/cookbook/templating/twig_extension.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this</a> link for more information). This function will check if the given string a valid route name:</p>
<pre><code>function routeExists($name)
{
    // I assume that you have a link to the container in your twig extension class
    $router = $this-&gt;container-&gt;get('router');
    return (null === $router-&gt;getRouteCollection()-&gt;get($name)) ? false : true;
}
</code></pre>
<p>But I'm not sure if this is a good idea to handle navigation in such way (using the database). Maybe you'd rather use something else?</p>
